WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.729 --> 00:00:04.850
You can't make a great horror movie without
also making a few mistakes.

00:00:04.850 --> 00:00:09.570
The final girl bursts out laughing during
her big escape scene; the blood-spewing machine

00:00:09.570 --> 00:00:14.650
malfunctions and saturates the entire set;
the flesh-eating swamp monster trips over

00:00:14.650 --> 00:00:17.720
his own tentacles and falls down a flight
of stairs.

00:00:17.720 --> 00:00:22.089
Sometimes these clips get relegated to the
gag reel, while in other cases they're so

00:00:22.089 --> 00:00:24.350
good they end up in the final film.

00:00:24.350 --> 00:00:28.769
Either way, here's a look at some great bloopers
that will change the way you see these horror

00:00:28.769 --> 00:00:29.960
movies.

00:00:29.960 --> 00:00:31.499
The Cabin in the Woods

00:00:31.499 --> 00:00:36.870
Joss Whedon's 2012 entry into the horror genre
was typically tongue-in-cheek, filled with

00:00:36.870 --> 00:00:41.550
intentional, hilarious subversions of various
scary movie tropes — including the epic

00:00:41.550 --> 00:00:46.840
finale, in which a virtual encyclopedia of
monsters escape from their cells and annihilate

00:00:46.840 --> 00:00:49.540
the technicians who've been holding them captive.

00:00:49.540 --> 00:00:54.239
But while the carnage of that last act was
planned, one of its best scenes was the beneficiary

00:00:54.239 --> 00:00:55.739
of a happy little accident.

00:00:55.739 --> 00:01:00.399
Specifically, we're talking about the scene
where actor Bradley Whitford is eaten by the

00:01:00.399 --> 00:01:01.399
merman.

00:01:01.400 --> 00:01:03.980
The scene itself was cool, but the best part
is what comes after.

00:01:05.960 --> 00:01:06.960
"Ah, come on…"

00:01:12.790 --> 00:01:15.300
The blowhole shooting is hilarious.

00:01:15.300 --> 00:01:18.340
But it's also not what the filmmakers originally
planned.

00:01:18.340 --> 00:01:22.410
With only the one scene to shoot, the effects
crew decided to use their entire remaining

00:01:22.410 --> 00:01:23.880
supply of fake blood.

00:01:23.880 --> 00:01:28.740
So instead of a little burp of blood, the
merman blew like Old Faithful—and kept on

00:01:28.740 --> 00:01:35.410
blowing, until the blood ran out and the geyser-like
effect was replaced by a farty red mist.

00:01:35.410 --> 00:01:40.980
Effects master David LeRoy Anderson of AFX
later said, "I love the wide shot in the behind-the-scenes

00:01:40.980 --> 00:01:44.650
video where the blood keeps going and going,
because it reminds me of that night, which

00:01:44.650 --> 00:01:45.690
was just hysterical.

00:01:45.690 --> 00:01:48.360
I kept thinking, 'How are they going to use
this?

00:01:48.360 --> 00:01:52.610
He's sitting there flapping like a fish, and
it looks like a hose spraying blood everywhere!'

00:01:52.610 --> 00:01:55.810
But the way they cut it together was perfect."

00:01:55.810 --> 00:01:56.810
Scream

00:01:56.810 --> 00:02:02.620
In 1996, Wes Craven's sendup of the slasher
genre heralded the dawn of a new wave of smart,

00:02:02.620 --> 00:02:04.460
sleek, self-aware horror films.

00:02:04.460 --> 00:02:08.509
The special effects, however, were the same
tried-and-true practical techniques directors

00:02:08.509 --> 00:02:13.180
have relied on for years, including the use
of corn syrup to simulate blood.

00:02:13.180 --> 00:02:17.340
And in a movie where it seemed like someone
was stabbed every other minute, things

00:02:17.340 --> 00:02:22.340
were extremely sloppy and sticky on set by
the time the film reached its thrilling climax.

00:02:22.340 --> 00:02:27.340
This led to a hilarious unplanned exchange,
when Skeet Ulrich lost control of the blood-covered

00:02:27.340 --> 00:02:31.799
phone and accidentally winged it right at
Matthew Lillard's head, leading to a very

00:02:31.799 --> 00:02:34.689
genuine reaction from the surprised actor.

00:02:34.689 --> 00:02:35.689
"Ahh.

00:02:35.689 --> 00:02:39.409
F------ hit me with the phone, D---!"

00:02:39.409 --> 00:02:44.390
Ordinarily, an outburst like that might have
led to a shout of "Cut!" and a request to

00:02:44.390 --> 00:02:45.390
do the scene again.

00:02:45.390 --> 00:02:49.459
But according to the Scream DVD commentary,
because Lillard was supposed to be playing

00:02:49.459 --> 00:02:54.859
the doofy sidekick to Ulrich's cold-blooded
psychopath, his reaction wasn't out of character.

00:02:54.859 --> 00:02:57.709
Craven went ahead and kept it safely off the
cutting room floor.

00:02:57.709 --> 00:03:02.200
As it turned out, it was a wise move; not
only did the line make it to the final cut,

00:03:02.200 --> 00:03:04.680
it's one of the funniest moments in the movie.

00:03:04.680 --> 00:03:08.560
Another of the funniest moments in Scream
can only be seen in the blooper reel, though,

00:03:08.560 --> 00:03:11.019
and it comes courtesy of the director himself.

00:03:11.019 --> 00:03:15.370
Wes Craven, who also directed the classic
A Nightmare on Elm Street, made a cameo in

00:03:15.370 --> 00:03:18.180
Scream dressed as Nightmare villain Freddy
Krueger.

00:03:18.180 --> 00:03:23.700
That was fun enough, but in one outtake, he
a gift for physical comedy that fans wish

00:03:23.700 --> 00:03:25.020
had made the final film.

00:03:30.680 --> 00:03:31.680
Scream 3

00:03:31.680 --> 00:03:36.120
The third entry in the Scream franchise was
also improved by an on-camera mistake.

00:03:36.120 --> 00:03:41.219
The exciting conclusion to Wes Craven's Scream
trilogy is full of scripted suspense, but

00:03:41.219 --> 00:03:45.650
one of its most action-packed fight scenes
has a big blooper right in the middle.

00:03:45.650 --> 00:03:50.220
According to an encyclopedic collection of
Scream 3 trivia, the confrontation between

00:03:50.220 --> 00:03:55.170
Neve Campbell and Scott Foley includes an
actual, genuine stabbing, in the moment where

00:03:55.170 --> 00:03:59.320
Sidney leaps over a bar and nails Roman in
the back with an ice pick.

00:04:05.280 --> 00:04:09.459
Foley was wearing a protective pad for the
scene, but Campbell missed her mark and plunged

00:04:09.459 --> 00:04:11.599
the pick into Foley's actual flesh.

00:04:11.599 --> 00:04:15.540
No wonder his scream of surprise and pain
seems so genuine!

00:04:15.540 --> 00:04:16.950
The Descent

00:04:16.950 --> 00:04:21.530
A terrifying movie in which a bunch of young
women are stalked and slayed while exploring

00:04:21.530 --> 00:04:27.170
a darkened cave system gets even more frightening
when The Descent adds in a bunch of subterranean

00:04:27.170 --> 00:04:30.230
monsters want to eat their delicious flesh.

00:04:30.230 --> 00:04:34.090
That's why it's so funny on the blooper reel
when one of the victims, whose face is all

00:04:34.090 --> 00:04:40.920
deformed from unspeakable things, gives one
of the humans an unexpected moment of romance.

00:04:40.920 --> 00:04:43.020
"Love you.."

00:04:46.000 --> 00:04:47.000
House of Wax

00:04:47.000 --> 00:04:53.410
The 2005 remake of the '50s horror classic
House of Wax starred WB heartthrobs such as

00:04:53.410 --> 00:04:58.910
Chad Michael Murray from One Tree Hill, Jared
Padalecki from Gilmore Girls…and socialite,

00:04:58.910 --> 00:05:02.260
reality star, and night vision camera owner
Paris Hilton.

00:05:02.260 --> 00:05:06.480
To her credit, the often dispassionate Hilton
gives everything she's got to her performance

00:05:06.480 --> 00:05:10.040
as a scream queen, shrieking 
as the script requires.

00:05:10.040 --> 00:05:14.601
The screaming is intentionally annoying, but
still not nearly as annoying as actual the

00:05:14.601 --> 00:05:18.480
car alarm that went off during a scene in
the woods, ruining the shot.

00:05:24.540 --> 00:05:25.770
Scream 4

00:05:25.770 --> 00:05:29.910
Acting can be magical when a director gets
a perfect, believable reaction from a performer

00:05:29.910 --> 00:05:33.470
— like one of abject terror in a horror
movie, for example.

00:05:33.470 --> 00:05:38.150
Or, you can just pull a prank on an actor
on a set of a horror movie and scare him for

00:05:38.150 --> 00:05:39.150
real.

00:05:39.150 --> 00:05:44.320
On the set of Scream 4, Erik Knudsen was apparently
supposed to open a door and find nothing there.

00:05:44.320 --> 00:05:48.640
Instead of nothing, however, there was something
— something actually pretty frightening,

00:05:48.640 --> 00:05:52.300
especially if you're not expecting it.

00:05:52.300 --> 00:05:53.160
"Ahh S---!"

00:05:56.580 --> 00:05:57.580
Halloween

00:05:57.580 --> 00:06:02.560
Star Malcolm McDowell is always an imposing
presence who dominates every scene he's in,

00:06:02.560 --> 00:06:05.710
whether he's playing the hero, an antihero,
or a villain.

00:06:05.710 --> 00:06:12.060
In Rob Zombie's 2007 version of Halloween,
he plays Dr. Samuel Loomis, the former psychiatrist

00:06:12.060 --> 00:06:14.210
of the crazed psycho, Michael Myers.

00:06:14.210 --> 00:06:18.680
Myers eventually comes for Dr. Loomis, of
course, and he cowers in fear in a darkened

00:06:18.680 --> 00:06:19.680
house.

00:06:19.680 --> 00:06:24.240
But when Myers smashes through the door to
get him, McDowell seems taken off guard.

00:06:24.280 --> 00:06:27.320
Apparently he didn't realize they were filming
that bit yet.

00:06:30.520 --> 00:06:31.980
"You must be f------ joking!"

00:06:34.260 --> 00:06:38.340
That Halloween reboot must have been a pretty
lively set to work on, because its blooper

00:06:38.340 --> 00:06:40.710
reel offers up another goofy outtake.

00:06:40.710 --> 00:06:42.460
What's so funny about being stabbed?

00:06:42.460 --> 00:06:45.860
As far as actor Ken Foree is concerned, everything.

00:06:45.860 --> 00:06:50.800
While Michael Myers repeatedly stabs him with
a prop knife and fake blood audibly oozes

00:06:50.800 --> 00:06:54.540
everywhere, Foree gets a case of the giggles
that simply won't die.

00:07:02.310 --> 00:07:03.500
Jennifer's Body

00:07:03.500 --> 00:07:08.060
Oscar winner Diablo Cody wrote the screenplay
for Jennifer's Body, which offered character

00:07:08.060 --> 00:07:12.140
relationships a bit more complex than those
in the average horror movie.

00:07:12.140 --> 00:07:16.650
Over the course of the film, nerdy Anita,
played by Amanda Seyfried, comes to both love

00:07:16.650 --> 00:07:22.380
and hate her best friend, popular cheerleader-turned
fatal succubus Jennifer, played by Megan

00:07:22.380 --> 00:07:23.380
Fox.

00:07:23.380 --> 00:07:27.630
Those mixed feelings physically manifest in
a scene in which Seyfried screams accusatory

00:07:27.630 --> 00:07:30.600
things at Fox's character…and then kisses
her.

00:07:30.620 --> 00:07:35.420
Or at least she tries to kiss her, as Fox
is apparently so deep into her monstrous character

00:07:35.420 --> 00:07:38.580
that she takes a bite out of her costar.

00:07:40.920 --> 00:07:43.040
"I actually bit her.

00:07:43.040 --> 00:07:44.980
I'm sorry."

00:07:44.980 --> 00:07:45.980
The Witch

00:07:45.980 --> 00:07:49.370
One of the most truly haunting horror movies
in years was The Witch.

00:07:49.370 --> 00:07:54.270
It features an atmospheric setting in colonial
Massachusetts, and it's paired with the scary

00:07:54.270 --> 00:07:58.590
premise that the witches of the Salem Witch
Trial era just might have been real.

00:07:58.590 --> 00:08:03.030
There's tons of weird stuff in The Witch,
from dark woods to kidnapping to naked people

00:08:03.030 --> 00:08:08.070
drinking blood to a goat named Black Phillip
that a pair of creepy twins says talks to

00:08:08.070 --> 00:08:09.070
them.

00:08:09.070 --> 00:08:10.320
But what's not so scary, though?

00:08:10.320 --> 00:08:11.320
Horses.

00:08:11.320 --> 00:08:15.140
Particularly horses needing to go about their
horse bodily functions with no regard for

00:08:15.140 --> 00:08:18.660
the very expensive film production happening
right in front of them.

00:08:20.280 --> 00:08:23.380
"If you don't let me alone with ya, I'll wake
mother and father this instant."

00:08:28.300 --> 00:08:30.300
The Silence of the Lambs

00:08:30.300 --> 00:08:35.079
Anthony Hopkins deservedly won an Academy
Award for Best Actor for his performance as

00:08:35.079 --> 00:08:38.409
cannibalistic psychopath Hannibal Lecter
in The Silence of the Lambs.

00:08:38.409 --> 00:08:43.370
Famously, it was one of only a handful of
horror movies to ever take home major Oscars.

00:08:43.370 --> 00:08:48.440
Hopkins is one the best actors in the world,
and as such, is quite versatile — he played

00:08:48.440 --> 00:08:53.399
an American president in Nixon, and a repressed
English butler in The Remains of the Day.

00:08:53.399 --> 00:08:55.560
He even played Rocky Balboa once.

00:08:55.560 --> 00:08:57.110
No, really, he did.

00:08:57.110 --> 00:09:01.050
While his face and shirt were covered in blood
during a twisted and hilarious outtake on

00:09:01.050 --> 00:09:05.800
the set of The Silence of the Lambs, he brought
his inner Rocky out for the world to see.

00:09:05.800 --> 00:09:08.180
"This one's for you Adrian.

00:09:08.180 --> 00:09:09.610
Not you, Pauly.

00:09:09.610 --> 00:09:11.019
Let's go for it.

00:09:11.019 --> 00:09:13.970
Rocky V. Let's do it now.

00:09:13.970 --> 00:09:16.089
That goes on the F------ box."

00:09:16.089 --> 00:09:18.410
Even cannibals need to laugh now and then.

00:09:18.410 --> 00:09:19.730
Shaun of the Dead

00:09:19.730 --> 00:09:24.120
Zombie-driven horror comedy Shaun of the Dead
made a movie star out of Simon Pegg.

00:09:24.120 --> 00:09:29.899
It also reunited the actor with his collaborators
from the cult British sitcom Spaced, including

00:09:29.899 --> 00:09:33.050
director Edgar Wright and costar Nick Frost.

00:09:33.050 --> 00:09:36.899
They're all good friends and seem to share
the same comedy hive mind, which means Pegg

00:09:36.899 --> 00:09:41.529
and Frost frequently ad-libbed and goofed
off on the set of Shaun of the Dead, ruining

00:09:41.529 --> 00:09:44.800
takes but cracking up each other and anybody
else in the vicinity.

00:09:44.800 --> 00:09:47.640
"Oh ah over here over here over here…

00:09:47.640 --> 00:09:48.640
Oh bullocks.

00:09:49.180 --> 00:09:50.180
Ok, ah..

00:09:50.180 --> 00:09:51.180
F--- it.

00:09:51.180 --> 00:09:52.180
F--- off.

00:09:52.180 --> 00:09:53.259
Back the f---- up."

00:09:53.259 --> 00:09:57.079
Now, why don't Rick and the rest of the gang
on Walking Dead just try that next time?

00:09:57.079 --> 00:09:58.430
Thanks for watching!

00:09:58.430 --> 00:10:01.389
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:10:01.389 --> 00:10:03.630
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

